   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`, which prints one `DATE: TEXT` line per note. It has a unit test, and the project checks pass: 2 tests ran and the line-length check is clean.\n\n- **Date format:** `DATE` is the date part of the stored timestamp, for example `2026-01-02: first`. `list` prints the full ISO timestamp. If you'd rather `export` show the full timestamp too, that's a one-line change.\n- **Code:** the command is in `fieldnotes/cli.py`. I also moved the usage string into one `USAGE` constant that now mentions `export`.\n- **Test:** the new test is in `tests/test_cli.py`. It adds two notes and checks the exact output lines.\n- **Running the checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set and fails without it. I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory.",
